<title>NETHERLANDS: Delta Lloyd Bank cuts Nedlloyd to Hold.</title>
<headline>Delta Lloyd Bank cuts Nedlloyd to Hold.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of April 1 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>Nedlloyd	  Transport     47.30   Delta Lloyd Bank</p>
<p>COMMENT: Hold (from Buy). EPS estimates for 1997 and 1998 downgraded mainly due to stronger than expected price pressure in shipping. Estimates assume 10 pct annual tariff erosion and 4 pct annual volume rise. Nedlloyd does not expect a loss, but no firm forecast probably until May shareholders meeting. Outperformance unlikely before then.</p>
<p>Future profit development very dependent on tariffs on Europe-Asia trade (40 pct of Nedlloyd's shipped volume). Positive factors include lower dollar transaction risk after P&amp;O container merger and effect of improved German economy on land transport activities.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     2.16     -	-     1.25</p>
<p>    1997		  4.25    11.1   2.5    1.50</p>
<p>    1998		  6.84    6.9    2.1    2.50</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
